  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Two crates of human fossils left Beijing and vanished. Inside were bones from at least forty individuals, dug out of a place called Dragon Bone Hill.",
        "visual_query": "wooden crate storage warehouse",
        "visual_fallback": "wooden crates"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Zhoukoudian had produced the best early-human collection on earth. In 1941, with Japan closing in, China sent it to New York for safekeeping.",
        "visual_query": "limestone cave excavation hillside",
        "visual_fallback": "cave dig"
      },
      {
        "narration": "US Marines were to load the footlockers onto the liner President Harrison. The ship never made port. Japanese warships attacked it and ran it aground.",
        "visual_query": "old cargo ship harbour",
        "visual_fallback": "cargo ship"
      },
      {
        "narration": "They left the medical college on the fourth of December, 1941, and were never reliably seen again. Sunk at sea? Ground up for medicine?",
        "visual_query": "foggy chinese city street",
        "visual_fallback": "empty street"
      },
      {
        "narration": "One marine said he dug up a box of bones at Qinhuangdao in 1947. A port researcher reckons the likely spot is under a parking lot.",
        "visual_query": "empty parking lot asphalt",
        "visual_fallback": "asphalt lot"
      }
    ],
